---
title: "Columns Tool Panel"
enterprise: true
---

The Columns Tool Panel provides controls for managing the grid's columns. Use it to show, hide and reorder columns, group rows, aggregate data and pivot.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tool Panel Simple" name="simple"  exampleHeight=630 /%}

{% note %}
Columns can only be dragged into a section when their column definition allows it: set `enableRowGroup` for grouping, `enableValue` for aggregation and `enablePivot` for pivoting.
{% /note %}

## Columns Tool Panel Sections

The Columns Tool Panel is split into the following sections, from top to bottom:

- Top area
    - **Pivot Mode Section**: Toggle to turn [Pivot Mode](./pivoting/) on or off.
    - **Expand / Collapse All**: Toggle to expand or collapse all column groups.
- **Columns Section**
    - Lists every column available to the grid, grouped by column group. By default the order matches the order of the columns in the grid; see [Suppress Column Reordering](./tool-panel-columns-layout/#suppress-column-reordering) to change this.
    - **Select / Unselect All**: Toggle to select or unselect all columns in the section.
    - **Select / Unselect Column (or Group)**: Select each column individually. The [Selection Action](#selection-action) depends on pivot mode.
    - **Drag Handle**: Drag a column, with the mouse or by touch, to one of the following:
        1. Row Groups Section
        1. Values Section
        1. Column Labels (Pivot) Section
        1. Onto the grid, which makes the column visible. Requires the grid option `allowDragFromColumnsToolPanel`.
        1. Elsewhere in the Columns Section, to reorder columns
- **Row Groups Section**
    - Columns here form the grid's [Row Grouping](./grouping/).
- **Values Section**
    - Columns here form the grid's [Aggregations](./aggregation/). The section follows the Excel naming convention of 'Values'.
- **Column Labels (Pivot) Section**
    - Columns here form the grid's [Pivot](./pivoting/). The section follows the Excel naming convention of 'Column Labels'.
- **Context Menu**
    - Right-click a column to open a menu for grouping, aggregating and pivoting it. See [Context Menu](./tool-panel-columns-customising/#context-menu).

{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/screenshot.png" alt="AG Grid Tool Panel Section" centered=true constrained=true width="46rem" /%}

## Selection Action

What selecting a column does depends on whether the grid is in pivot mode:

- **Pivot Mode Off**: Selecting a column toggles its visibility. A selected column is visible and an unselected column is hidden.
- **Pivot Mode On**: Selecting a column groups, aggregates or pivots it, depending on what the column allows.

